1. Configuring your DNS servers to only respond to authorized queries.
2. Implementing rate limiting and filtering to prevent amplification attacks.
3. Keeping your DNS servers and other systems up-to-date with the latest security patches.
4. Educating yourself and others about the risks of DNS amplification attacks and how to prevent them.

